From 026b15af269fe23d32939f1b300dcf0be858a87d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:30:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fat-tier MoE glue: one token pass for the gate/up input
 Hadamards, activation in the up epilogue

- exl3_had_r_128_token_gate_up: each token's row of x (bf16 or fp16) is read
  once, rounded to fp16 as x.half() does, and written pre-scaled by the
  expert's gate/up suh and Hadamard-transformed to every fat route row; it can
  also zero the fp32 routed accumulator. Replaces x.half(), the zero fill and
  two gathered exl3_had_r_128_grouped launches.
- exl3_fat_gemm_grouped_act: the up projection's epilogue reads the gate rows
  and applies clamp + activation + fp16 round + down-suh Hadamard, replacing
  exl3_act_had_r_128_grouped and the fp32 up buffer.
- apply_exl3_fused_moe: per-expert counts read to the host once; when every
  routed expert is fat the layer goes straight to the fat tier (no fp16 copy of
  x, no zero fill, no empty standard launch). The fp16 copy is made lazily.

Bit-identical intermediates (tests in test_fat_gemm_grouped.py); routed output
differs only by atomic order. Real 16K-chunk routing, 57 layers: 78.9 -> 72.5 ms
per layer (tests/gpu/bench_fat_glue.py).
