 ### Changed
 
+- Fat-tier MoE glue (prefill): the gate and up input Hadamards run as one pass over the tokens
+  (`exl3_had_r_128_token_gate_up`: each token's bf16 row is read once and written, pre-scaled per
+  expert, to all its fat route rows; it also zeroes the fp32 routed accumulator), and the up
+  projection's epilogue applies clamp + activation + fp16 round + down-input Hadamard
+  (`exl3_fat_gemm_grouped_act`), replacing the act pass and the fp32 up buffer. When every routed
+  expert is fat (`VLLM_EXL3_FAT_THRESHOLD_PREFILL=0`) the layer skips the fp16 copy of x, the
+  separate zero fill and the empty standard launch; the per-expert row counts are read once.
+  Every intermediate is bit-identical to before; the routed output differs only by atomic
+  accumulation order (max |diff| 2.4e-7). Real MiniMax-M3.1 16K-chunk routing, 57 layers, 2.15
+  pack shapes: 78.9 -> 72.5 ms per layer (token pass -4.3 ms, activation epilogue -2.1 ms);
+  `tests/gpu/bench_fat_glue.py`.
+
 - Grouped fat-expert GEMM (`exl3_fat_gemm_grouped`): A rows and trellis words now stream
   global -> shared with `cp.async` through a 5-stage pipeline (4 for K >= 4) of 32-wide K
   stages instead of a register-staged 64-wide prefetch, with one barrier per stage placed so
